      "answer": "$P=(-1,m)$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$mx+c=-\\frac mx$, hence $mx^2+cx+m=0$ — M1. All $x$ terms in numerator; OE.\nFor one intersection, $b^2-4ac=0$, hence $c^2-4m^2=0$ — M1; discriminant condition may be implied.\n$c=\\pm2m$ — A1; SOI, allow $\\pm$ here.\nSubstitute $c=+2m$: $mx^2+2mx+m=0$, hence $x^2+2x+1=0$ — M1; ignore substitution of $-2m$.\n$(x+1)^2=0$, hence $x=-1$ only — A1.\n$y=m$ only, giving $P=(-1,m)$ — A1.\nAlternative differentiation: $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac m{x^2}$ — M1; equate to $m$ and solve $x^2=1$ — M1 A1; select $x=-1$ only and find $y$ — M1 A1; same point — A1. Total: 6.",
