      "answer": "$Q=\\left(m^2,-\\frac1m\\right)$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Normal through their $P$ with gradient $-\\frac1m$: $y-m=-\\frac1m(x+1)$ — *M1; OE, coordinates of $P$ must be in terms of $m$ only. Allow use of negative reciprocal of their curve gradient at $P$.\nEquate normal to $y=-\\frac mx$ and remove denominator, obtaining $x^2+x(1-m^2)-m^2=0$ — DM1; OE.\n$(x+1)(x-m^2)=0$, hence the other intersection has $x=m^2$ — A1; quadratic-formula equivalent accepted.\n$y=-\\frac{m}{m^2}=-\\frac1m$, hence $Q=(m^2,-\\frac1m)$ — A1; ignore coordinates of $P$. Total: 4.",
